// Use VdfqLanguage.pkg // Which language VDFQuery's own texts use
//
// It follows DataFlex's own setting, Language$Current (LanguageText.pkg and Language_Current.inc), so a program has one
// language setting and not two. A copy of Language_Current.inc that the compiler finds before the installed one picks
// another language, and DataFlex ships those files under Usr\Language.
//
// VDFQuery holds texts for the ten languages named below. With any other setting its texts are English. #IFSAME compares
// the names instead of calculating with them, so a setting that was never defined takes that same path and does not stop
// the compile: DataFlex's Czech files name Language$Czech, and LanguageText.pkg does not define it.
Use LanguageText.pkg

#IFSAME Language$Current Language$English Language$Nederlands Language$Svenska Language$Deutsch Language$Dansk Language$Portugues Language$Francais Language$Italiano Language$Espanol Language$Norsk
 Define VDFQ_Language For Language$Current
#ELSE
 Define VDFQ_Language For Language$English
#ENDIF
